## Key Issues Fixed

> [!WARNING]
> **Port Conflict Resolved**: Both `kryptos-server` and `kryptos-client` were hardcoded to port 8080. Client moved to port 3000.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **ESM/CJS Conflict Handled**: Root [package.json](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/package.json) has `"type": "module"` but PM2 config and orchestrator require CommonJS. Solved by using [.cjs](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/ecosystem.config.cjs) extensions for both infrastructure files.

## Commands Reference

### One-Command Startup
```bash
npm start                    # Development mode (all services)
npm run start:cloud          # Cloud mode (server + bridge only)
npm run start:local          # Local node mode (full mesh)
```

### PM2 Direct
```bash
pm2 start ecosystem.config.cjs          # Start all
pm2 start ecosystem.config.cjs --only kryptos-server   # Single service
pm2 list                                # Status table
pm2 logs                                # Live logs
pm2 logs kryptos-bridge                # Single service logs
pm2 restart kryptos-server             # Restart one
pm2 stop all                            # Stop all
```

### Orchestrator Commands
```bash
node kryptos-orchestrator.cjs                  # Full boot sequence
node kryptos-orchestrator.cjs --mode=cloud     # Cloud mode
node kryptos-orchestrator.cjs --health         # Health check only
node kryptos-orchestrator.cjs --status         # Service status
node kryptos-orchestrator.cjs --stop           # Stop everything
```

